## Groth16 verifier template  (MIT — Remco Bloemen)

The bn254 Groth16 verifier contracts were generated from Remco Bloemen's Solidity verifier
template and remain under the MIT license. Each file carries an in-file `@author Remco Bloemen`
attribution. They are:

- `src/rayls-protocol/Enygma/Enygma-Payments/EnygmaVerifierk{2,3,4,5,6}.sol`
- `src/rayls-protocol/Enygma/Enygma-Payments/EnygmaDepositToDvpVerifierk{2,3,4,5,6}.sol`
- `src/rayls-protocol/Enygma/Enygma-Payments/EnygmaWithdrawFromDvpVerifierk{2,3,4,5,6}.sol`
- `src/rayls-protocol/Enygma/Enygma-DVP/EnygmaJoinSplitVerifier.sol`
- `src/rayls-protocol/Enygma/Enygma-DVP/Erc1155JoinSplitVerifier.sol`
- `src/rayls-protocol/Enygma/Enygma-DVP/Erc721OwnershipVerifier.sol`

## Baby JubJub curve  (MIT — iden3 / yondonfu)

`src/rayls-protocol/Enygma/Enygma-Payments/CurveBabyJubJub.sol` is a Baby JubJub
elliptic-curve implementation derived from <https://github.com/yondonfu/sol-baby-jubjub>
(originally iden3), under the MIT license.

## Build dependencies

The contracts are compiled against third-party libraries consumed as package dependencies,
each of which retains its own license — notably **OpenZeppelin Contracts** and
**OpenZeppelin Contracts Upgradeable** (MIT) and **poseidon-solidity** (MIT). These are
declared in `package.json`; the Poseidon hash contracts under `src/rayls-protocol/Enygma/`
are thin Rayls wrappers that re-export `poseidon-solidity`.

